tar Storm Conventions that started in NWO revised. It also has amazing rules for voidship creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I myself haven't played or read any MtA books but I own some for my OWoD collection, but hope one day to run a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:11:10-07:00","id":987180,"title":"","content":"I second Clanbook: Baali. The opening fiction is disgusting but well done, in a Clive Barker kind of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T05:44:05-07:00","id":987209,"title":"","content":"The Half-Damned: Dhampyr book from KotE. It is the best of the minor supernatural books (followed by World of Darkness: Sorcerer).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:25:41-07:00","id":988447,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages: Europe<br /> The Guide to the High and Low clans<br /> The Road Books<br /> <br /> I think those are among my favorites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T02:26:24-07:00","id":988750,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages: Europe is pretty good, I would have liked to see more books done in that style for different time periods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:30:07-07:00","id":989147,"title":"","content":"(How does DA: Europe qualify as a splat book? Location books aren't splat books; that's a term for a book devoted to a particular character type)<br /> <br /> Dharma Book: Devil Tigers. What looks to be an edgy and flashy romp through highly sexualized ultraviolence is actually a statement on how to be a suitably grandiose, yet still definitely disturbing and wicked, devil figure. Spoilers: the target is Willy Wonka, or somewhere around him. That's the clear image of what you're going for: offering up temptation and punishing those who take the bait with cleverly ironic means that highlight the shortcomings and transgressions as the very thing that did them in or caused their fall from grace. Musical numbers expounding on this performed by demons ritually bound to the character are strictly optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:19:38-07:00","id":989181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986816-favorite-owod-splat-book?p=989147#post989147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(How does DA: Europe qualify as a splat book? Location books aren't splat books; that's a term for a book devoted to a particular character type)</div> </div> </div> </div>The term splat book has been used to cover any non-core sourcebook, but originally yes it was coined in regards to White Wolf's *book the asterisk being replaced by the appropriate term (clan, tribe, tradition, etc). I mentioned Dark Ages: Europe because it had been previously mentioned and I really like the book.<br /> <br /> That said if you want an answer more close matching the original definition I would say Sorcerer, Revised Edition. It had unawakened magic that still felt cool and interesting as well as providing some brief ideas for sorcerous organizations. I could easily see myself playing a game with nothing but Sorcerers and having a lot of fun with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:44:01-07:00","id":989404,"title":"","content":"Would you say that Sorcerer: Revised is better than Sorcerer: The Hedge Magician's Handbook? I think to prefer the latter over the former, but that is a personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T10:24:43-07:00","id":989423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986816-favorite-owod-splat-book?p=989404#post989404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you say that Sorcerer: Revised is better than Sorcerer: The Hedge Magician's Handbook? I think to prefer the latter over the former, but that is a personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer Sorcerer, Revised Edition for the following reasons<ul><li>I think the rules in Revised are better presented and structured. I feel like I could successfully make my own Path based on the rules presented in Revised if I had to good idea as a base</li> <li>I love the Aspect system for constructing effects if gives flexibility within a Path while also making each spell have a touch of uniqueness</li> <li>I like that they included Psychic powers in addition to more classic sorcery</li> <li>While Hedge Magician's Handbook might have a few organizations better fleshed out, I preferred the way they presented a bunch of organizations in Revised, as well as ways to connect the rules to True Mages (both Traditions and Technocracy)</li> <li>Overall I felt that Revised benefited from time and refinement on the systems providing what I feel is a better system to use</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:05:00-07:00","id":989440,"title":"","content":"Tribebook: Shadow Lords. Pure unfiltered pro-Subterfuge propaganda. My first and favorite Tribebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:12:40-07:00","id":989448,"title":"","content":"Dharma book: Devil Tigers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:57:18-07:00","id":989474,"title":"","content":"Technocracy: Progenitors it got me past thinking the Technocracy was more than just Hit Marks and MiB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:01:07-07:00","id":989475,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it qualifies as a true splat book (though its definitely a &quot;splatter book&quot;), but Freak Legion has always been an all time favorite. In a pretty thin book it makes Fomori interesting and compelling without removing any of their horror, while still cramming in enough crunch to support a playable Fomori game in its own right. Is it so 90's it hurts? Definitely, but it has a raw sincerity to it that makes it hard to hold that against it. Is it pretty tasteless at points? Yeah, but the revulsion it evokes is part of what keeps the Fomori monstrous while adding nuance and humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:43:33-07:00","id":989578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986816-favorite-owod-splat-book?p=989475#post989475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it qualifies as a true splat book (though its definitely a &quot;splatter book&quot;), but Freak Legion has always been an all time favorite. In a pretty thin book it makes Fomori interesting and compelling without removing any of their horror, while still cramming in enough crunch to support a playable Fomori game in its own right. Is it so 90's it hurts? Definitely, but it has a raw sincerity to it that makes it hard to hold that against it. Is it pretty tasteless at points? Yeah, but the revulsion it evokes is part of what keeps the Fomori monstrous while adding nuance and humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love Freak Legion.<br /> <br /> That's probably my favorite, along with Hunter the Reckoning: Wayward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:16:56-07:00","id":989860,"title":"","content":"I tend to prefer Possessed over Freak Legion because it makes better characters and more interesting enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:51:11-07:00","id":989900,"title":"","content":"I found Possessed very dry in comparison to Freak Legion. Including a larger variety of spirit-possessed options beyond Fomori is a plus, but it also dilutes the overall feel of the book. I can also understand walking back some of the Black Dog elements, but that also takes away from the uniqueness that Freak Legion had. Not saying Possessed is an inferior book, just not my preference by a long shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:04:31-07:00","id":989932,"title":"","content":"Possessed doesn't have a dark and fun splatterpunk comic at the beginning that reels you in while simultaneously disgusting you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:08:13-07:00","id":989969,"title":"","content":"Nothing quite like opening that front page for the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:01:12-07:00","id":990324,"title":"","content":"There's a pretty consistent theme here: people prefer the later rules and the mid-90s fluff. Likewise, most people seem to prefer the really violent/dark stuff (Devil Tigers, Baali, Freak Legion). That's interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:05:10-07:00","id":990327,"title":"","content":"Oh, how could I forget: Dark Reflections: Spectres (even despite *that* infamous pic).<br /> <br /> Less dark but still incredibly cool: Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> And for old times' sake: Ghouls: Fatal Addiction (much better than the new ghouls book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T03:33:03-07:00","id":990359,"title":"","content":"Memory is getting fuzzy on my CWoD days but I'd say Dark Ages: Fae and Guide to the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:54:54-07:00","id":990520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986816-favorite-owod-splat-book?p=990324#post990324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a pretty consistent theme here: people prefer the later rules and the mid-90s fluff. Likewise, most people seem to prefer the really violent/dark stuff (Devil Tigers, Baali, Freak Legion). That's interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only speaking for myself, I like Baali and GFA because I feel it shows the potential of how VtM can be a horror game, but not in a cheesy type of way.<br /> <br /> Not to knock other story styles, but I am not really a fan of the super hero with fangs, katana blades and pony tail types of games. I like the personal horror type. Not as much as the flesh cathedral type stuff, but more so the corrupting type. The first story arc in my game simply deals with Ghouls, and that is enough. How mortals are corrupted by it. Baali, well Baali if done right can be awesome, but I have found so many people abuse the Baali theme to where it loses it touch. IMO no player should play a baali, and if one is used by a ST it should be in very minute measures for the largest impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:56:27-07:00","id":990522,"title":"","content":"Oh and in GFA addiction the template for the dog handler I found brought up a sickening since of dread and horror, as did the opening scene in Clanbook Baali, I mean shit I almost quit reading because I felt I shouldn't be fucking read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:17:30-07:00","id":990676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986816-favorite-owod-splat-book?p=990324#post990324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a pretty consistent theme here: people prefer the later rules and the mid-90s fluff. Likewise, most people seem to prefer the really violent/dark stuff (Devil Tigers, Baali, Freak Legion). That's interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom comes from pain, and Devil Tigers made us very wise...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T17:23:42-07:00","id":990703,"title":"","content":"Well, it is the World of Darkess. I would not mind, however, if someone had a WoD game about something positive. Perhaps something involving magical bunnies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T01:32:12-07:00","id":990858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986816-favorite-owod-splat-book?p=990703#post990703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is the World of Darkess. I would not mind, however, if someone had a WoD game about something positive. Perhaps something involving magical bunnies...</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling?<br /> <br /> Personally, the most appealing games for me explore a variety of styles. I like the dark cathedrals of flesh stuff mostly, too, but I like personal horror and occasionally vampions. Heck, I *liked* Dirty Secrets. But more for its conspiracies and eldritch horrors than its kewl powers.<br /> <br /> The Baali are totally playable, though. Never say never is my rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T08:15:48-07:00","id":990968,"title":"","content":"Each to their own, but there are some things I never allow in my games, and PC Baali are at the top of that list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T09:38:49-07:00","id":990991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986816-favorite-owod-splat-book?p=990858#post990858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changeling?<br /> <br /> Personally, the most appealing games for me explore a variety of styles. I like the dark cathedrals of flesh stuff mostly, too, but I like personal horror and occasionally vampions. Heck, I *liked* Dirty Secrets. But more for its conspiracies and eldritch horrors than its kewl powers.<br /> <br /> The Baali are totally playable, though. Never say never is my rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I respect every type of story being told, because in the end that's the whole system, I myself prefer to keeps some things as mysterious as can be. Not saying there is a wrong or right stance, but I wouldn't allow players playing Baali.<br /> <br /> I mean heck, I only allowed the 7 core clans in my game. I just prefer to take really small aspects of the game, and expand on them, and very slowly introduce other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" 